{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>You are stationed this day before YHWH your Elohim.</b> And whoever would mislead me cannot mislead him (i.e., each individual's own understanding), and upon his understanding you accept upon yourselves." "<b>Your heads, your tribes, your elders, and your officers.</b> Your heads — that is, your tribes: the ruling tribes. They are the princes and officers in whose hand is the ruling tribe." "<b>Your elders.</b> These are the judges." "<b>Your officers.</b> Who have authority to compel the litigants. And upon all these heads it is incumbent to instruct the multitude what is good for them to accept or to refuse."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The comment addresses the switch to singular address: each person stands individually accountable, so that no one can be misled through another. The Hebrew is elliptical and rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:28.963538255Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}